# ChronoRoute colouring rules. Wireshark uses the FIRST rule that matches.
# Format: @name@display filter@[background R,G,B][foreground R,G,B], 16-bit colour values
# (background first: Wireshark's own "@UDP@udp@[56026,61166,65535][4718,10030,11796]" is
# dark text on light blue). tshark -T psml --color shows the result; a test checks it.
@T-CRH malformed@tcrh.valid == 0@[0,0,0][65535,65535,0]
@T-CRH deviation (DEV)@tcrh.flags.dev == 1@[52428,0,0][65535,65535,65535]
@T-CRH late at capture@tcrh.late == 1@[65535,42405,0][0,0,0]
@T-CRH on schedule@tcrh@[52428,59110,65535][0,0,0]
@CRH (RFC 9631)@ipv6.routing.type in {5, 6}@[59110,59110,59110][0,0,0]
